# Security baseline

These rules apply to **every** change. The verifier (Layer 3c) checks them on every task.

## Secrets

- **Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or any file containing real secrets.** Only `.env.example` (key names, no values) is allowed.
- **Never paste secret values** into code, comments, docs, or chat output.
- All secrets come from **Infisical**:
  - Local dev: `infisical run --env=development -- <command>`
  - CI: Infisical OIDC actions, env-scoped
  - Fly runtime: Infisical → Fly secret sync
- Required Infisical envs: `development`, `staging`, `production`. Never share values across envs.
- **Adding a new env var?** Follow the four-step Infisical-first workflow in `05-env-vars-infisical.mdc`. Partial registration (e.g. code references the var but Infisical doesn't have it) fails Layer 3c verification.

## Logging

Never log any of:

- `password`, `passwordHash`
- `accessToken`, `refreshToken`, full `Authorization` headers, full cookies
- `JWT_*`, `*_SECRET`, raw `DATABASE_URL` (redact query string)

Pino redact list must cover all of the above. Sentry `beforeSend` drops the same fields.

## Auth

- Access tokens: JWT bearer, **15 min** TTL, signed with `JWT_ACCESS_SECRET`.
- Refresh tokens: HttpOnly + Secure + SameSite=Strict cookie, path `/auth/refresh` only, 30-day TTL, rotated on every refresh.
- Client stores access token in **memory only** — never `localStorage` or `sessionStorage`.
- bcrypt cost factor 12 for password hashing.
- WS auth: JWT in `socket.handshake.auth.token`; per-socket expiry timer; `AUTH_REFRESH` over open socket.

## Input handling

- All REST bodies validated by `class-validator` DTOs (`whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true`).
- All WS payloads parsed by Zod; reject malformed with `ACTION_REJECTED`.
- Sanitize every free-text field that can render in HTML (chat, station name, vehicle name, dispatch center name, alliance name + description, vehicle category labels) — strip `<`, `>`, `<script>`.
- All DB queries via **Prisma** parameterised methods. No raw SQL outside reviewed migrations.
- Every mutation checks the JWT `playerId` matches the resource owner (or verified alliance membership).

## Network

- HTTPS everywhere; HSTS on production.
- CORS allowlist per env (Infisical) — never `*`.
- Helmet on backend with strict CSP; map tile origin allowlisted.
- WebSocket `Origin` header validated against the same allowlist.
- Rate limiting per `engineering §10`.

## Anti-patterns

```typescript
// ❌ logging secrets
logger.info({ token: accessToken, user });

// ❌ token in localStorage
localStorage.setItem('access_token', token);

// ❌ raw SQL with interpolation
prisma.$queryRawUnsafe(`SELECT * FROM players WHERE id = '${id}'`);

// ✅ parameterised
prisma.player.findUnique({ where: { id } });
```
